====== ZBT WR8305RT ======

{{section>meta:infobox:432_warning#infobox_for_dataentries&noheader&nofooter&noeditbutton}}

The ZBT WR8305RT is a 802.11bgn wireless router based on the [[https://wikidevi.com/wiki/MediaTek_MT7620|MediaTek MT7620N]] SoC. It has five Ethernet ports, out of which one is the wan port. It has one radio (SoC-based 2.4 GHz 802.11bgn). It comes pre-installed with OpenWrt Chaos Calmer.

The PCB has a label of [[toh:zbtlink:we526|ZBT-WE1626]], which is probably the internal name of the router, whereas it is marketed as ZBT WR8305RT.

zbt we3826 is 8mb version of wr8305rt (openwrt image from wr8305rt succesfully installed via uboot and 1st lan port)

{{:media:zbt:zbt_wr8305rt_top.jpg?400|ZBT WR8305RT (Top View)}}

